==Oni Summary==
Main goals whilst playing Oni
# Get {{ItemTooltip|Berzerker}} (and preferably {{ItemTooltip|Cataclysm}} as well) before you play Oni. They don't need to be legendary.
# Cast {{SpellTooltip|Furious Strike}} in a loop whilst in Defense stance (~170% "Furious Strike" charges per second.) 
# Fast burst
# Scry summons
# Stack Incants until you can make profits. 
# Level up your {{PetTooltip|Interrogator}} to increase {{SpellTooltip|Possessed Blade}}
# Stack up lots of {{SpellTooltip|Furious Strike}}
# Charge {{ItemTooltip|Cataclysm}} weapon. 
# Level {{PetTooltip|Voidterror}} to gather '''Void Mana'''
# Level Burst Pet to '''Burst'''
{{SummarizeGuideBoxSets}}

==Phases==
===Step 1: Scry your Summons===
Utilize {{ItemTooltip|Shadow-Scryer's Crystal Ball}} and summoning duration reduction to stack {{SpellTooltip|Summon Horned Incinerator}} and {{SpellTooltip|Summon Infernal Thrasher}}, and get some Void Entities at the same time.

Upon initiating a new Exile, remember to switch to {{StanceTooltip|Meditation}} Stance to acquire a single charge for {{SpellTooltip|Temper The Steel}}. After your TTS has sufficient FS charge speed, then switch to {{StanceTooltip|Defense}} Stance.

Once you've unlocked [[Phylactery|Phylacteries]] at [[Paragon]] 29, use {{PetTooltip|Ley Keeper}} to massively boost your phylactery power.  Before then use {{PetTooltip|Archivist}} to boost evocation efficiency on SE. If charge generation is too slow, use {{PetTooltip|Ent}} to boost the effectiveness of {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}}.

To achieve the required 30 Dominance to equip Ent, you can use {{ItemTooltip|Commissar's Torn Sleeve}} or {{ItemTooltip|Voidstrike Seal}}.

{{GuideBox|pet=Archivist|pet1=Ley Keeper|spells=#0#SummonScry@21,2;28,2;11,2;71,2;86,2;87,2|stance=Defense|itemtab=Items|items=#0#SummonScry@101;115;0;24;12;32;41;64;56;83;72;1023;212;300;414;415;90;2003;3008;509|note= The only enchants that matter are on Pants and Cold Blooded Ring. Items with an Evocation Efficiency enchant can be enchanted once to be left at level 1.}}

This phase only needs a few minutes, until the evo bonus on SHI slows down.

===Step 2: Berzerker Buildup===
Stack Incants by using Berzerker in Defense with 100% cast rate, variable length.

Do a quick burst (Cataclysm Stacking, Vmana phase, Burst) to gain more sources. Optionally, max out your amount of Monuments using Simulacrum or Greater Chimera with {{ItemTooltip|Collar Of Obedience}} and {{ItemTooltip|Whiplash}}. More Monuments = More Incants from Berzerker. You can easily add those items to the Cataclysm charge item loadout and do it there, since it has an open belt and ring slot.  

Once you have access to {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Scabbard}} (E360 Mysteries) and can hit 45 casts per second on Furious Strike without {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}} on the bar, swap it to {{SpellTooltip|Unclean Knowledge}}.   

This phase lasts as long as needed for profits. Pet doesn't particularly matter, so early on Pixie is used for autoclicks, level it with [[#General Pet Levelling|Burst Pet Levelling Set]].  After [[Phylactery|Phylacteries]] are unlocked at e450 mysteries, {{PetTooltip|Ley Keeper}} will provide a slight increase to cast rate, both through its own bonus Mastery and the level reduction increasing Phylactery power. If you are running {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}} and still cannot hit max cast speed, use {{PetTooltip|Ent}}.

{{GuideBox|pet=Pixie|pet1=Ent|spells=#1#BerzerkerBuildup@60,2;21,2;88,0;89,0;86,2;87,2|stance=Defense|note=Unequip Searing Gaze if it breaks your 100% Defense stacking uptime.|t-spells=without CGE|t-spells1=CGE|items=#1#BerzerkerBuildup@101;113;4;24;17;31;46;69;58;88;77;1011;209;308;414;415;90;2001;3002;502|itemtab=Max CAP}}

====Offline====
If going offline in this phase, make certain that IB/ES have a non-zero cast rate before saving ('enter' hotkey can be helpful).  If you save at the wrong time, you could potentially return to no casts having been performed.  Potentially make several exports to reduce the chances of getting a dud.  If going offline for longer than a day, don't forget to equip {{ItemTooltip|Light Of Eighth Star}}.

===Step 3: Box Levelling Phase===
Level{{PetTooltip|pet_name=Interrogator}} high to boost {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Possessed Blade}}. Refill spells using {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Force Of Will}} with {{StanceTooltip|Meditation}} as needed. Once leveling speed slows down, simply go to the next step. 

{{GuideBox|pet=Interrogator|t-spells=Meditative Fury|spells=#2#BoxLevel@64,2;63,2;88,2;117,2;107,2;28,2|t-spells1=Force Of Will|spells1=#2#BoxLevel(beforeMF)@64,2;63,2;88,2;91,2;107,2;28,2|stance=Berserk|items=#2#BoxLevel@104;113;6;23;18;32;41;68;57;84;76;1002;211;301;411;405;91;2002;3003;509}}

===Step 4: Stack Furious Strike===
Use {{SpellTooltip|Temper The Steel}} to stack all the charges of {{SpellTooltip|Furious Strike}} that you'll use in Burst. {{SpellTooltip|Furious Strike|FS}} doesn't need to be on the spellbar for this, so feel free to replace it if needed.

You can also use this phase in Meditation stance to charge up IB, ES and PB at the start of the exile, that way you'll have charges to sustain other phases.

{{GuideBox|pet=Ent|
spells=#3#FS_Stack@21,2;107,2;88,2;89,0;86,0;87,2|
items=#3#FS_Stack@106;113;9;27;13;33;43;61;57;87;76;1001;208;302;406;402;90;2009;3007;506|stance=Berserk|note=Only enchant charge speed and summoning efficiency items}}
To level Ent you can use [[#General Pet Levelling|Levelling Burst Pet]] with {{ItemTooltip|Commissar's Torn Sleeve}} and/or {{ItemTooltip|Voidstrike Seal}} to get the 30 Dominance required.

The evocation scaling of {{SpellTooltip|Temper The Steel}} is additive to the casts scaling, and thus much less effective.  Maximizing Charge Speed and Summoning Efficiency to boost the power of {{SpellTooltip|Conjure Greater Elemental}} are the most noteworthy increases in charge speed.

Stack for up to 10% of your exile, but make sure to check how many charges you have from time to time, it caps at 1 billion charges(1e9). However, Oni executes several bursts in sequence. Accumulating an overabundance of charges prior to the final burst will probably yield no benefit.

===Step 5: Cataclysm Charging Phase===
Charge Cataclysm as high as possible with Evo/Inc Reduction Items

{{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Meditative Fury}} gives more stacks and scales alongside mysteries earned. Before unlocking {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Meditative Fury}}, use {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Iron Blood}} in its place. 

Make sure your {{SpellTooltip|spell_name = Meditative Fury}} usage rate is <1/s by using incant reduction gear, evo reduction increases stacks from amount of Hellstorm casts and fireball.

Pet and items outside of the ones listed should not matter. If the duration of your incantation spells is higher than 1, you can equip any item with Character ability power bonuses and use Ley Keeper or Geode to increase the bonus of the Defense stance. 

You can equip {{ItemTooltip|Collar Of Obedience}} and {{ItemTooltip|Whiplash}} here if you want to have a loadout to max sources with. Just equip {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Simulacrum}} or {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Greater Chimaera}} alongside those items and wait. 

{{GuideBox|t-spells=Meditative Fury|spells=#4#ChargeCataclysm@64,2;2,2;6,2;117,2;28,2;11,2|t-spells1=Iron Blood|spells1=#4#ChargeCataclysm(beforeMF)@64,2;2,2;6,2;88,2;28,2;11,2|stance=Defense|items=#4#ChargeCataclysm@101;-1;-1;-1;-1;-1;-1;-1;58;-1;77;1002;209;-1;-1;-1;-1;2002;-1;-1}}

