==In-Depth Mechanics==
===TTS Math===
<details open>
<summary>TTS Math</summary>
<div>
To maintain the loop, {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Temper The Steel}} must be fully refunded by casting all granted {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Furious Strike|display_name=Furious Strikes}}. This is possible when:
<br><math>C \times R \times 1.1^{S} \geq \frac{N}{T}</math>

E.g. when {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Temper The Steel}} grants '''170%''' {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Furious Strike}} charges per second, and casting charge-based evocation spells shares '''11.5%''' of their cost.

{{ItemTooltip|item_name=Searing Gaze}} will '''halve''' {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Temper The Steel}} duration and thus '''double''' the loop threshold. {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Scabbard}} will reduce the loop threshold by '''10%''' (multiplicatively) per enchant.

where:
* <math>C = \text{FS Charges from TTS Each Second}</math>
* <math>R = \text{TTS Charge Share}\,\%</math>
* <math>S = \text{Temporal Scabbard Enchant Level}</math>
* <math>N = \text{Charging Evocations on Panel}</math>
* <math>T = \text{TTS Duration}</math>
</div>
</details>

===Tips===
*As {{ClassTooltip|class_name=Apprentice}}, get some easy {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Spellhound}} levels with {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Spell Focus}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Magic Missile}} before switching to {{ClassTooltip|Oni}}. This can let you quickly cast {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Unclean Knowledge}} and {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Ritual Of Power}} to get started.
* With enough enchants on {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Temporal Scabbard}}, the start phases can be skipped. Don't forget to level a buildup pet!
*Do an early burst for Upgrades and faster Source Maxing.
*If using {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Hungerer}} in the [[#Burst_2|Burst]] phase, do ''not'' buy any sources in the [[#Pre-Burst|Pre-Burst]] phase. Before and after your first {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Furious Strike}}, buy max [[Sources#Hellhole_-_Demonologist|Hellholes]] and any Upgrades. Continue buying Upgrades, but not sources.
*At 1e780 mana (1e384 [[Mysteries]]), {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Meditative Fury}} becomes available. Use it in place of {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Force Of Will}} everywhere, to boost Pet Ability Power and {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Cataclysm}} stacking. At low [[Attributes#Wisdom|Wisdom]], periodic manual casts of {{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Force Of Will}} may still be necessary to refill spells.
*At higher Memories equip incant/evo duration reducing items during buildup with Muscle Memory to get slightly more RoP/UK/TTS casts
*After your first burst you can go back to {{PetTooltip|Greater Chimaera}} to build up some sources you couldn't afford during burst
*If going offline make sure you equip {{ItemTooltip|Light Of Eighth Star}} (Dust cap) and {{ItemTooltip|Blessed Tapestry}} (Attribute speed).

===High Mysteries===
<!--TODO: split into second guide-->
At higher [[Mysteries]] we gain access to T3 pets and the [[Pantheon]] ([[Memetics]] will not change our strategy).

{{SpellTooltip|spell_name=Meditative Fury}} improves {{ItemTooltip|item_name=Cataclysm}} stacking further. 

'''Pets'''
*{{PetTooltip|pet_name=Living Sin}} > {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Hungerer}} burst pet, level for 25 seconds.
*{{PetTooltip|pet_name=Greater Chimaera}} > {{PetTooltip|pet_name=Simulacrum}} for Source stacking.

'''Build up'''
*You can get around 10% more RoP and UK casts with maxed Muscle Memory, Kata bracers, Searing Gaze, Frosty ring, Habitstone. Rest of items can be enchanted with CAP to increase it more. If you have plenty of Iron Blood stacks you could use them up to cast more too.

'''Cataclysm''' 
*You want to make sure you get as many casts as possible of both Fireball and Hellstorm, so equipping items like Searing Gaze, and Warp Basilisk will increase overall stacks. Make sure to try to press Cataclysm when all non summon spells are about to cast at the same time (If you swap spell set, usually after 4 casts of MF & UK they will be decently timed).

